              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Charlotte"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used to work for Arctic Circle before they automated everything; we made the secret fry sauce from scratch back then.\n\nThis is almost it! For the restaurant, we would've omitted the pepper; added a little paprika, and a little mustard."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Doddie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this sauce for labor day to go on my grilled burgers. I added finely diced red onion. OMG!! Everyone loved this sauce. Definitely will make again.",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-04T00:03:08.860Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SneakySpud3324"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am adding what I did for those who need to watch their Sodium \"Salt\" intake. I use the No-Salt Added Ketchup (which is 5mg per tablespoon) and this sauce tastes great! My Mom used to like the sauces offered in restaurants but needed a low-salt diet; I made this for her and she loved it!",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-25T10:03:01.726Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Maria Joy Schrock"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow, this sauce is the reason I make burgers! The only change I make is to use 1 clove fresh garlic instead of garlic powder. I also pat the chopped dill pickles dry with a paper towel so it doesn't get so runny!",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-25T13:22:07.713Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Captain Awesome"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Add some chopped onion and a dash of worcestershire sauce. Really steps up the game",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-25T12:55:36.583Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MugRug"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The best! I also use green pickle relish instead of pickles, as I did not have pickles the first time I made it. (I also only use about 1/4 cup)Delish! Always requested at BBQ ‘s. Thank you for the recipe! It’s a hit with everyone.",
            "datePublished": "2019-06-15T19:00:26.017Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DanielleLyn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This makes a great burger sauce! This is similar to another recipe that I make, but this one is a little less sweet. I did use sweet relish in place of the chopped dill pickles. I also added in some finely minced onion. It does taste better when it marinates an hour or two in the fridge. It spruces up any ordinary burger! Thank you for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-23T00:18:01.557Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "grizken"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are classic ingredients. Not tough to memorize, and then select the amount of ea ingredient that you prefer to your own taste. I like Miracle Whip, vs Mayo. I like using dill pickle relish, for consistancy vs. chopping pickles and making a watery mess. When in a big rush, I thin out a little bottled Thousand Island sald dressing, adding a tablespoon or two of the whip or mayo. I have to have this on so much diff. foods... one of my staple substances!",
            "datePublished": "2023-08-17T21:09:28.115Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "fear no food"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is easier than a dallas cowboy cheerleader after a 12 pack! I didn't use regular ketchup. I used jalapeno ketchup by heinz and deleted the black pepper. I also used a 1/4 teaspoon of minced garlic instead of garlic powder I didn't have any powder. I also put the chopped pickles on a napkin to dry. Boars head pickle chopped. Now for the burgers I used 90/10 hamburger with 1 tablespoon of A1, 1/2 tablespoon of worcestershire sauce. Then I put the burgers in a 6 count muffin pan for 30 mins at 350. We like our burgers a little rare. Everybody on this holiday weekend loved it!!",
            "datePublished": "2014-05-24T15:47:22.943Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
